+# G7.2 2026-08-29: ON. Austin named HOD and LOD as two of his six levels, and
+# HOD alone is the engine's single biggest level miss -- 413 symbol-days where
+# a human named it and the engine had no level for it
+# (research/corpus_sf/level_grading.md). The July A/B that switched this off
+# measured it at the staleness settings below, which made it nearly dead: 85
+# trades in two years and zero extra S days (research/g72_sixlevels_report.md).
+HODLOD_PAIR = os.getenv("HODLOD_PAIR", "1").strip().lower() in ("1", "true", "yes", "on")
+# How stale the session extreme has to be to count as a break-and-retest level.
+# It has to be SOME way stale -- a level you break and retest must have been set
+# before the retest window, or the pattern cannot exist -- so the 12-bar FSM
+# window is the floor. The old 43/30 pair was not about the pattern: it was
+# chosen so the HOD would not duplicate the OPENING RANGE high, which pushed
+# the first possible HOD entry out to 10:13 on a session that ends at 11:00.
+HODLOD_MIN_BARS = int(os.getenv("HODLOD_MIN_BARS", "20"))    # was 43
+HODLOD_MIN_AGE = int(os.getenv("HODLOD_MIN_AGE", "12"))      # was 30

